    "text": "{\n  \"semantic_type\": \"dimension\",\n  \"unit\": null,\n  \"additive_over_entities\": null,\n  \"additive_over_time\": null,\n  \"time_rollup\": null,\n  \"valid_methods\": [],\n  \"period_basis\": \"mixed\",\n  \"derivation\": \"End date of the reporting period for each XBRL fact, as reported in the SEC companyfacts filing. It is the balance-sheet date for instant facts and the last day of the quarter or year-to-date window for duration facts.\",\n  \"calendar\": null,\n  \"seasonal_adjustment\": \"n/a\",\n  \"annualized\": null,\n  \"entity_grain\": null,\n  \"hierarchy\": null,\n  \"comparability\": null,\n  \"lineage\": {\n    \"url_template\": \"https://data.sec.gov/api/xbrl/companyfacts/CIK{cik}.json\"\n  },\n  \"description\": \"Date on which the reporting period of a fundamentals fact ends. It is a time dimension and is not meant to be aggregated. Rows mix instant, quarterly (Q) and year-to-date (YTD6, YTD9) period bases. Fiscal calendars differ by company: Darden (DRI) uses fiscal quarter-ends that fall on dates such as 2026-02-22, while Yum (YUM) and Chipotle (CMG) report on calendar quarter-ends. Use it together with period_start and period_basis to tell periods apart.\"\n}",
